        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f48695824c724f459bfda1a0959aa75e",
      "statement": "Findings live in PostgreSQL under the pull request they were raised on (owned by FindingState/FindingRow models); legacy findings before migration to PostgreSQL still exist in thread metadata and are copied over on first access, marked by a pull_request_finding_state row.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/review/findings.py#L1-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e4e22f8eb23c172abe3cfb98bd5291e46f07ea1ee00f3dfb5230273c31fe7bb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5f840e3acfcc4c91bd31a8f9ff5ba716",
      "statement": "Persisted finding records are normalized on every read by _normalize_publication_identity, which folds legacy flat-singular GitHub-identity fields and a nested 'surface' record into the canonical comment/thread id lists plus surface_state so the rest of the codebase never sees the legacy shape.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/review/findings.py#L369-L410",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab02afa550793903376312568670fd782145c75e5ce5e3c7a5f259395c4401bf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c1455f351194f3390b1101ff8da4471",
      "statement": "Findings writes go through a locked read-modify-write layer: mutate_findings reads the freshest list and only persists when the mutator reports a change, replace_findings merges an incoming snapshot by id so concurrently-added findings are not dropped, and append_finding de-duplicates by fingerprint against open findings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/review/findings.py#L946-L1005",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a14ca487639ad45a1c1ab64ee4834552167d8a7df4a6fd381d06bc2ac7db222e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d9ce4798cd543ad90ca5d82230e861f",
      "statement": "When the reviewer thread backing findings storage does not exist, the storage layer raises ReviewerThreadMissingError and tools return a structured do-not-retry result (thread_missing_tool_result) instead of blindly retrying.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://openswe/review/findings.py#L48-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9963ae40c15e611cd3bb7f40004af4c77664d240181d3c7448410fe8810105bc:"
        },
        {
